3110..3185 Comment "/// Spinning undoes winding at every word: the round trip at a variable, by"
3186..3260 Comment "/// induction over the presented words. The result type reads the word the"
3261..3332 Comment "/// fold descends on, so each arm answers it at its constructor and the"
3333..3391 Comment "/// recursive call at the field: `sectWords[<](x)` relates"
3392..3467 Comment "/// `spinWords(windWords(x))` to `x`, and carried along `around` it relates"
3468..3542 Comment "/// `Loop(spinWords(windWords(x)))`, which `spinWords(windWords(Loop(x)))`"
3543..3620 Comment "/// runs to, to `Loop(x)`. The case respects both rules: at `Loop(Unloop(x))`"
3621..3695 Comment "/// the arms compose to `cong(around, cong(unaround, p))`, whose functions"
3696..3772 Comment "/// compose to the identity under the rules, so the chain is `p` itself, the"
3773..3791 Comment "/// answer at `x`."
